package: zigbee
description: Silicon Labs implementation of the Works With All Hubs connectivity functions per the Zigbee WWAH Requirements document. This component should be included by routers and end devices only. This component manages connectivity states to both the hub and, for end devices, to the parent. In the event of connection loss, restoration is performed per the WWAH Connectivity Recovery Procedure as defined in the Zigbee WWAH Requirements specification. The component uses the Trust Center Keepalive component on routers and non-sleepy end devices to determine hub connectivity. On sleepy end devices, it uses the Poll Control Server component to determine hub connectivity. On end devices, this component also uses the End Device Support component to determine parent connectivity.
label: SL Works With All Hubs Connectivity Manager
quality: production
id: zigbee_wwah_connectivity_manager
category: Zigbee|Works With All Hubs
provides:
- name: zigbee_wwah_connectivity_manager
requires:
- name: zigbee_tc_connectivity
recommends:
- id: zigbee_trust_center_keepalive
  vendor: silabs
config_file:
- path: app/framework/plugin/wwah-connectivity-manager/config/wwah-connectivity-manager-config.h
source:
- path: app/framework/plugin/wwah-connectivity-manager/wwah-connectivity-manager.c
- path: app/framework/plugin/wwah-connectivity-manager/wwah-connectivity-manager-cli.c
  condition:
  - cli
include:
- path: app/framework/plugin/wwah-connectivity-manager
  file_list:
  - path: wwah-connectivity-manager.h
  - path: wwah-connectivity-manager-tokens.h
template_contribution:
- name: component_catalog
  value: zigbee_wwah_connectivity_manager
- name: zigbee_stack_callback
  value:
    callback_type: stack_status
    function_name: sl_zigbee_af_wwah_connectivity_manager_stack_status_cb
- name: cli_group
  value:
    group: plugin
    name: wwah-connectivity-manager
    help: wwah-connectivity-manager related commands.
- name: cli_command
  value:
    group: wwah-connectivity-manager
    name: info
    handler: sli_zigbee_af_wwah_connectivity_manager_info_command
    help: Prints information about the WWAH Connectivity Manager state.
- name: cli_command
  value:
    group: wwah-connectivity-manager
    name: enable
    handler: sli_zigbee_af_wwah_connectivity_manager_enable_command
    help: Enables the WWAH Connectivity Manager rejoin algorithm.
    argument:
    - type: uint8
      help: The endpoint that contains WWAH cluster
- name: cli_command
  value:
    group: wwah-connectivity-manager
    name: disable
    handler: sli_zigbee_af_wwah_connectivity_manager_disable_command
    help: Disables the WWAH Connectivity Manager rejoin algorithm.
    argument:
    - type: uint8
      help: The endpoint that contains WWAH cluster
- name: cli_command
  value:
    group: wwah-connectivity-manager
    name: show
    handler: sli_zigbee_af_wwah_connectivity_manager_show_command
    help: Shows the WWAH Connectivity Manager rejoin algorithms parameters.
- name: cli_command
  value:
    group: wwah-connectivity-manager
    name: parent-recovery
    handler: sli_zigbee_af_wwah_connectivity_manager_bad_parent_recovery_command
    help: Disables/enables the WWAH bad parent recovery. And sets the bad parent check and rejoin period (min), if enabled.
    argument:
    - type: uint8
      help: Disable ==0, enable == 1, the WWAH bad parent recovery
    - type: uint16
      help: the Period of time after which we check if a parent is bad and try rejoin if so. 0 means use the default value of 24 * 60 mins.
- name: cli_command
  value:
    group: wwah-connectivity-manager
    name: min-rssi
    handler: sli_zigbee_af_wwah_connectivity_manager_set_min_rssi_command
    help: Sets minimum acceptable RSSI for receiving packets on an SoC WWAH-enabled device.
    argument:
    - type: int8
      help: min acceptable RSSI value for receiving packets
- name: token_header
  value: wwah-connectivity-manager-tokens.h
documentation:
  docset: zigbee
  document: zigbee-af-api/wwah-connectivity-manager
metadata:
  sbom:
    license: MSLA
root_path: zigbee
